postings.description:
The role

You will own how technical knowledge is captured and turned into certified documentation across the AR5 product team. This is not passive writing or pure prompt engineering: you enable our product engineers to generate documentation directly from their own work using TEKEVER's internal LLM tools, while acting as the accountable human-in-the-loop who guarantees accuracy and compliance. In short, you are a force multiplier for the engineering team, making technical writing a by-product of engineering work rather than a downstream burden.

Location: Caldas da Rainha

What you will do

- Enable engineers to produce AR5 documentation with our internal LLM tools, providing the structure, templates, and review that turn raw knowledge into release-quality output;

- Act as the human-in-the-loop: validate and correct AI-generated content for technical accuracy and compliance with aerospace, defence, and UAS certification standards;

- Build and maintain documentation templates, authoring standards, and knowledge-capture practices (structured notes, design rationale) that feed our tooling;

- Govern the full AR5 documentation baseline: structure, version control, traceability, single source of truth;

- Collaborate across systems engineering, avionics/firmware, RF, payload (EO/IR, radar, AIS, SIGINT), and quality teams.

What you bring

- Degree in Aerospace, Electronic, Electrotechnical, or Systems Engineering, or similar;

- Proven experience in a technical role in aerospace, defence, or UAS/autonomous systems, such as documentation engineer, technical writer, or systems engineer;

- Knowledge of avionics, embedded systems, RF, and payload integration, and the ability to read schematics and protocols (MIL-STD, MAVLink, STANAG, or similar);

- Comfort with AI/LLM tooling, version control, and docs-as-code, or strong aptitude to adopt them;

- Excellent technical English, paired with the judgment to validate AI output.

What we have to offer you:

- An excellent work environment and an opportunity to make a difference;

- Salary Compatible with the level of proven experience.

- Daily shuttle from Leiria, Lisbon, Alcobaça and Rio Maior

Missão:

Desenvolvemos os moldes para com eles criarmos as peças que tornam os nossos UAVs possíveis. A nossa missão é inovar o processo, testar novos materiais, explorar novas técnicas e encontrar soluções de fabrico que simplifiquem o nosso trabalho, garantam a mais alta qualidade e elevem o desempenho de cada peça que sai das nossas mãos.

Localização: 100% presencial nas Caldas da Rainha

Quais serão as tuas principais responsabilidades:

- Desenvolvimento de moldes para a produção de peças em fibra de carbono;

- Desenvolvimento de masters para a produção de moldes em carbono;

- Elaboração de desenhos técnicos e respetiva documentação de apoio à produção e montagem, quando necessário;

- Acompanhamento na produção dos moldes bem como das peças;

- Colaboração com outras equipas para otimizar os processos de produção ao nível dos compósitos, novas abordagens, conceitos e procedimentos;

Perfil e Requisitos:

- Formação superior em Engenharia Mecânica, Aeroespacial, Automóvel, Aeronáutica ou áreas similares (obrigatório);

- Mínimo 1 ano de experiência profissional consolidada na área dos compósitos (obrigatório);

- Experiência em SolidWorks ou softwares similares, com maior foco na utilização de superficies (obrigatório);

- Domínio da lingua portuguesa e bons conhecimentos de inglês;

- Atitude proativa, dinamismo e vontade de aprender;

- Espírito de equipa e boa capacidade de comunicação;

- Atenção ao detalhe e rigor.

O que temos para te oferecer:

- Um ambiente de trabalho dinâmico e colaborativo, com oportunidade de gerar impacto real

- Subsídio de alimentação e seguro de saúde para os colaboradores

- Serviço de transporte (shuttle) para os escritórios em Leiria, Caldas da Rainha e Ponte de Sor

- Bónus de acordo com a política da empresa

- Acesso ao Employee Assistance Program (programa de apoio ao colaborador)

Se estás preparado(a) para abraçar esta oportunidade, envia-nos a tua candidatura

Mission:

Your mission will be to help transform ideas into reliable electronic systems that power the AR3.

You will contribute to the development and continuous improvement of electronic hardware, working across circuit design, prototyping, testing, validation and production implementation. You'll work hands-on with a complex UAV platform, solving real engineering challenges and seeing your designs become part of a product that actually flies.

Maybe you'll even learn how to fly the AR3!

Main Responsibilities:

- Support the development and continuous improvement of the AR3's electronic systems;

- Translate technical requirements into functional, reliable and manufacturable electronic designs;

- Design, prototype and validate electronic circuits and PCBs using EDA tools;

- Build, assemble and test electronic prototypes, iterating designs based on laboratory and field testing;

- Support product changes from circuit design through prototyping, validation and implementation into production;

- Troubleshoot electronic systems, perform root cause analysis and contribute to robust technical solutions;

- Collaborate closely with Mechanical, Software, Manufacturing and Quality teams to integrate electronic solutions into the final product;

- Consider manufacturability, testing and reliability throughout the electronic development process;

- Contribute to the continuous evolution of the AR3 platform.

Profile & Requirements:

- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Electronics Engineering, Electrical Engineering or a related field (mandatory);

- Experience with EDA tools such as Altium Designer, KiCad, Eagle or similar (preferred);

- Previous experience in electronics product development, PCB design, prototyping or a similar environment is valued;

- Knowledge of electronic circuit design, PCB development and debugging techniques;

- Familiarity with PCB manufacturing, soldering and electronic prototyping methods is valued;

- Knowledge of programming languages such as C/C++ and Python is valued;

- Good level of English (B2 or above); Portuguese is a plus;

- Hands-on mindset, with an interest in working directly with hardware, prototypes and laboratory testing;

- Proactive, curious and solution-oriented;

- Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail;

- Team player, comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities can evolve quickly.

What we have to offer you

• A dynamic and collaborative working environment, with the opportunity to make a real impact
• A competitive salary package, aligned with your proven level of experience
• Meal allowance and health insurance for employees
• Shuttle transport service to the offices in Leiria, Caldas da Rainha and Ponte de Sor
• Bonus in line with company policy
• Access to the Employee Assistance Programme (EAP)

