Mission

To ensure the accurate, safe, and efficient flow of materials and products throughout TEKEVER’s supply chain by managing receiving, storage, inventory, and shipping operations with excellence. We are committed to maintaining inventory integrity, supporting operational readiness, and delivering the right materials to the right place at the right time, enabling innovation and mission success across all TEKEVER programs.

What will be your responsibilities:

- Receiving Operations

- Inspect and verify incoming shipments against purchase orders or packing lists to ensure accuracy;

- Unload, sort, and store materials or products in designated areas within the warehouse;

- Report any discrepancies, damages, or quality issues with received goods;

- Maintain accurate records of received shipments in the inventory management system.

- Shipping Operations

- Prepare and package goods for shipment, ensuring proper labelling and documentation;

- Coordinate with carriers or couriers to schedule pickups;

- Inspect outgoing shipments to ensure they meet quality and order specifications;

- Generate shipping documents such as packing lists, transport documents and dangerous goods declarations.

- Inventory Management

- Perform inventory counts and cycle checks to ensure accuracy in stock levels;

- Update the inventory system with real-time data on received and shipped items.

- Equipment and Safety

- Operate forklifts, pallet jacks, and other material-handling equipment as required;

- Ensure adherence to safety protocols and proper handling of goods;

- Maintain a clean and organized workspace in compliance with health and safety standards.

Profile and Requirements:

- High school diploma or equivalent;

- Minimum 3 years of experience in a logistics, warehouse, or shipping/receiving role;

- Strong knowledge of shipping and receiving procedures and documentation;

- Ability to operate forklifts or other material-handling equipment;

- Dangerous Goods Certification for ADR/IATA will be considered a plus;

- Strong organizational and time-management skills;

- Attention to detail and accuracy in handling goods and records;

- Language Requirements: Advanced proficiency in Portuguese and English, with proven fluency at the C2 level in both languages;

- Team player and strong communication skills;

- Proficiency in inventory and warehouse management systems is a plus.

What we have to offer you:

- We offer an excellent work environment and an opportunity for you to make a difference;

- Salary compatible with the level of proven experience;

- Daily transport from the following locations (Leiria, Alcobaça, Rio Maior and Lisbon).

If you are ready to embrace this exciting journey, send us your application! ‍

